	(footprint "zxv:Jack_3.5mm_PJ-320D_TRS"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "824fd1b4-2c96-41dc-a6d7-5f13c86f71f6")
		(at 166 58.9 -90)
		(descr "PJ-320D 3.5 mm jack (4-pole TRRS, SMD, horizontal) WIRED AS TRS. Copied from the stock Jack_3.5mm_KoreanHropartsElec_PJ-320D-4A_Horizontal, whose geometry is drawn from the part datasheet (LCSC C95562), with two pads renamed: R1 becomes R, and R2 becomes a SECOND S. Why: the part has no switch contact (KiCad names those with an N suffix and calls this symbol Audio Jack, 4 Poles TRRS), so grounding the second ring is correct or harmless whether a 3-pole plug lands its sleeve on S, on R2, or across both - while leaving it floating fails in the case where the sleeve lands on R2 alone. This keeps the AudioJack3 symbol, so no schematic rewiring. LCSC C431535.")
